    "result_text": "Full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 1/1 test). Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe E.164 normalizer in `E164.java` validated only total digit count (8\u201315) but not the national-number length per country code. I added that check with minimal structural impact \u2014 one small file, one small helper, and a single extra condition on the existing guard:\n\n- **`NATIONAL_LENGTHS`** map: country calling code \u2192 required national digits (`\"61\"\u21929`, `\"1\"\u219210`).\n- **`nationalLengthValid(digits)`** \u2014 a self-contained helper that, when the digits carry a known country code, requires the national part (digits after the code) to be exactly the mandated length; unknown codes pass through unchanged.\n- **`toE164`** gains one clause: `... || !nationalLengthValid(digits)` on the existing reject branch, so a wrong length throws `InvalidTelephoneException` \u2192 HTTP 400.\n\n`E164` is a tiny class (WMC_other is near-zero), `toE164`'s complexity rose by one branch, and the new helper is small and cohesive \u2014 so structural cost stays low. The test `+61 123` (only 3 national digits, needs 9) now returns 400, while valid AU mobiles (`+61`+9) and NANP seed numbers (`+1`+10) still pass.",
